# curie_map:
#   skos: "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
#   semapv: "https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/"
#   eccdm: "https://hl7.eu/fhir/ig/cancer-common/element/"
#   osiris: "https://github.com/siric-osiris/OSIRIS/data-element/"
# mapping_set_id: "https://w3id.org/cancer-crosswalk/mappings/osiris__to__eccdm"
# mapping_set_title: "OSIRIS (inter-SiRIC oncology minimum data set, FR) -> ECCDM element crosswalk"
# mapping_set_version: "0.1.0"
# license: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
# mapping_tool: "semantic proposal (review pending)"
# mapping_provider: "https://w3id.org/cancer-crosswalk"
# subject_source: "https://github.com/siric-osiris/OSIRIS (data/DataElementConcept.tsv, master e76142b 2022-10-20; FHIR IG inca.fhir.uv.osiris 1.1.0)"
# object_source: "https://hl7.eu/fhir/ig/cancer-common"
# comment: "Direction: subject (OSIRIS) <predicate> object (ECCDM hub). Terminology deferred. OSIRIS is event-based: TumorPathologyEvent covers both the initial diagnosis and later loco-regional / metastatic events, so several items fan out to CancerConditionAtDiagnosis AND ClinicalCancerProgression (source_context = event role)."
subject_id	subject_label	subject_terminology	source_context	predicate_id	object_id	object_label	mapping_cardinality	element_kind	mapping_justification	confidence	review_status	comment
osiris:Patient_Gender	Gender	FHIR AdministrativeGender	—	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:CancerPatient.sexAtBirth	SexAtBirth	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.70	proposed	OSIRIS Patient_Gender is administrative gender (FHIR AdministrativeGender: M/F/UN); hub sexAtBirth is biological sex assigned at birth. Same value set, slightly different concept. observedSexGender has no OSIRIS counterpart — HUB GAP.
osiris:Patient_BirthDate	Birth Date	—	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerPatient.birthDate	BirthDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.95	proposed	Full date of birth on both sides.
osiris:Patient_DeathDate	Death Date	—	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:LastFollowUp.deathDate	DeathDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Date of death; OSIRIS keeps it on Patient, hub on LastFollowUp.
osiris:Patient_CauseOfDeath	Cause of death	UMLS C0007465	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:LastFollowUp.causeOfDeath	CauseOfDeath	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.85	proposed	Coded cause of death (UMLS concept in OSIRIS vs CodeableConcept in hub). Terminology alignment deferred.
osiris:Patient_LastNewsDate	Last News Date	—	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:LastFollowUp.date	Date	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Date of last news = date of last follow-up observation.
osiris:Patient_LastNewsStatus	Last News Status	OSIRIS LastNewsStatus	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:LastFollowUp.vitalStatus	VitalStatus	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Alive / deceased at last news; hub vitalStatus is Alive | Dead. evidenceOfDisease has no OSIRIS counterpart — HUB GAP.
osiris:RelatedPathology_PathologyCode	Pathology Code	ICD-10	—	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:CancerPatient.comorbiditiesAtCancerDiagnosis	ComorbiditiesAtCancerDiagnosis	n:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.70	proposed	OSIRIS RelatedPathology = coded non-cancer disease with diagnosis / end dates, not restricted to the time of cancer diagnosis. Hub collapses to a list of comorbidities present at diagnosis; OSIRIS dates (RelatedPathology_DiagnosisDate / PathologyEndDate) have no hub home.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_Type	Type	OSIRIS EventType	event role	skos:relatedMatch	eccdm:ClinicalCancerProgression.diseaseStatus	DiseaseStatus	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.50	proposed	OSIRIS event type (primary cancer, loco-regional recurrence, metastatic recurrence, ...) codes the kind of tumour event, not a remission / progression status. Related only.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_Type	Type	OSIRIS EventType	event extent	skos:relatedMatch	eccdm:ClinicalCancerProgression.extentType	ExtentType	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.55	proposed	The OSIRIS event-type value set also carries extent (local vs loco-regional vs metastatic), which is what hub extentType records. Same subject mapped twice because the OSIRIS concept conflates event role and extent.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_StartDate	Start Date	—	subsequent event	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:ClinicalCancerProgression.assertedDate	AssertedDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.65	proposed	For non-initial events the start date is the date the progression / recurrence was asserted. For the initial event see TumorPathologyEvent_DiagnosisDate.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_DiagnosisDate	Diagnosis Date	—	initial event	skos:broadMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.visitDate	VisitDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.65	proposed	One diagnosis date in OSIRIS vs four diagnostic-date subtypes in the hub (visit / biopsy / imaging / lab report). Mapped to visitDate as the most likely equivalent, as for oBDS and B1MG; the other three are HUB GAPS.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_HistologicalGradeType	Histological Grade Type	OSIRIS HistologicalGradeType	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.tumourGradeSystem	TumourGradeSystem	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Grading scale (e.g. SBR, Gleason, WHO) = hub grading system.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_HistologicalGradeValue	Histological Grade Value	OSIRIS HistologicalGradeValue	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.tumourGradeValue	TumourGradeValue	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Grade value under the chosen scale; OSIRIS mirrors the hub's system + value split.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_StadeType	Stade Type	OSIRIS StadeType	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.classificationType	ClassificationType	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.85	proposed	Stage classification scale (TNM stage grouping, FIGO, Ann Arbor, ...) = hub classificationType.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_StadeValue	Stade Value	OSIRIS StadeValue	stage group	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.stage.value	Stage element value	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	Overall stage value (e.g. IIA). Hub stage backbone holds one entry per axis; the stage group is one such entry (stage.code = overall stage).
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_TopographyCode	Topography Code	ICD-O-3 topography	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.bodySite	BodySite	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	ICD-O-3 topography of the primary tumour = hub primary site.
osiris:TumorPathologyEvent_MorphologyCode	Morphology Code	ICD-O-3 morphology	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.histologyBehaviour	HistologyBehaviour	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	ICD-O-3 morphology incl. behaviour digit = hub histologyBehaviour.
osiris:TNM_T	T	OSIRIS T_TNM	T	skos:broadMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.stage.value	Stage element value	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	T component value; axis identity (T) is implicit in the item name, no explicit stage.code counterpart — same coarseness as B1MG.
osiris:TNM_N	N	OSIRIS N_TNM	N	skos:broadMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.stage.value	Stage element value	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	N component value; see TNM_T.
osiris:TNM_M	M	OSIRIS M_TNM	M	skos:broadMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.stage.value	Stage element value	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	M component value; see TNM_T.
osiris:TNM_Version	TNM Version	OSIRIS TNMVersion	TNM	skos:relatedMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.classificationType	ClassificationType	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.55	proposed	TNM edition number implies the system (TNM) but does not name it; hub classificationType names the system.
osiris:TNM_Type	TNM Type	OSIRIS TNMType	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:CancerStage.type	Type	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.85	proposed	c / p / r / y prefix = clinical vs pathological staging in the hub (hub value set is Clinical | Pathological only, so r / y collapse).
osiris:ResponseEvaluation_Date	Date	—	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:OverallCancerTreatmentResponse.date	Date	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.90	proposed	Date of the response assessment.
osiris:ResponseEvaluation_Status	Status	OSIRIS RECIST	—	skos:exactMatch	eccdm:OverallCancerTreatmentResponse.treatmentResponseType	TreatmentResponseType	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.85	proposed	RECIST response category on both sides. OSIRIS links the evaluation to a Treatment, the hub to the condition / progression — reference axis differs.
osiris:Treatment_Type	Type	OSIRIS TreatmentType	—	skos:broadMatch	eccdm:SystemicTreatment.type	Type	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.60	proposed	OSIRIS Treatment_Type spans all modalities (surgery, radiotherapy, chemotherapy, ...) which are separate hub models; hub type is the kind of systemic treatment only. Cross-model scope collapse, as for B1MG.
osiris:Treatment_StartDate	Start Date	—	systemic	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:SystemicTreatment.startDate	StartDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	One generic treatment start date in OSIRIS; the hub splits by modality. Row per target model, discriminated by source_context (Treatment_Type value).
osiris:Treatment_StartDate	Start Date	—	radiotherapy	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:Radiotherapy.startDate	StartDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	See systemic row.
osiris:Treatment_StartDate	Start Date	—	surgery	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:Surgery.date	Date	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.70	proposed	Surgery has a single date in the hub; OSIRIS start date of a surgical treatment is that date.
osiris:Treatment_EndDate	End Date	—	systemic	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:SystemicTreatment.endDate	EndDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	See Treatment_StartDate. SystemicTreatment.ongoing has no OSIRIS counterpart — HUB GAP.
osiris:Treatment_EndDate	End Date	—	radiotherapy	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:Radiotherapy.endDate	EndDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	See Treatment_StartDate.
osiris:Treatment_ClinicalTrialContext	Clinical Trial Context	OSIRIS Boolean	—	skos:relatedMatch	eccdm:SystemicTreatment.setting	Setting	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.35	proposed	Weak: 'treatment given in a clinical-trial setting' is a context attribute, not the neoadjuvant / adjuvant setting the hub records. Kept to record the decision; intent and setting are otherwise HUB GAPS for OSIRIS.
osiris:Series_Modality	Modality	DICOM	—	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:Imaging.type	Type	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	DICOM modality (CT, MR, PT, ...) vs hub imaging procedure type; close, hub value set is procedure-oriented.
osiris:Series_BodyPartExamined	Body Part Examined	DICOM	—	skos:closeMatch	eccdm:Imaging.bodySite	BodySite	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.75	proposed	DICOM body part examined vs hub anatomical site(s) imaged.
osiris:Study_AcquisitionDate	Acquisition date	DICOM	—	skos:relatedMatch	eccdm:CancerConditionAtDiagnosis.imagingDate	ImagingDate	1:1	collected	semapv:LogicalReasoning	0.45	proposed	Hub imagingDate is the date of the diagnostic imaging supporting the diagnosis; a DICOM study date is that only for the diagnostic study. Hub Imaging model itself has no date — HUB GAP.
